			<div class="content" id="post-content-4805299">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Drama/Emotional, Action</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A serial killer with mind-reading abilities, able to predict all outcomes of an interaction he engages with someone, as well as the easiest and quickest ways to achieve them. He can also read an individual's entire life by reaching to their memories, obtaining enough information to lure them in any way. He had a simple life as a photographer, which allowed him to find victims more easily by taking photos of frequently visited places. Because of his superpowers, he always knew the perfect place, time and method to kill his victims without a trace.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The serial killer surrendered to a Foundation intelligence agency shortly after killing two of their agents who were working on the investigation of a series of disappearances in a specific region of the US, which he claimed to be responsible for. He demonstrates how his powers work live to the agents during a brief interrogation, confirming the existence of an anomaly case. However, even without posing any threat, because he proved to be responsible for a series of crimes that could otherwise lead to a severe court sentence, he was escorted to the Foundation by an MTF squad. He constantly offers himself to help the Foundation with several tasks, such as in investigative processes, containment of anomalies, and even janitorial work, trying to get the Foundation to grant all of his &quot;requests for individual rights&quot; (most of which, if not all, are denied).</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> He tells Foundation personnel that, upon a period of usage of his powers, he had developed a side effect: When accessing an individual's memory, he will quickly experience the feelings present in those memories so vividly that he can even feel their pain. This restricted him from killing by slowly bringing the desire to empathize with his victims, causing him to conflict with his own moral values. Because of that, when he discovered the Foundation through the memories of a field agent who he happened to pass by, he decided to change his killing methods in order to lure the Foundation's eyes. He surrendered to them on purpose, just so he would not need to use his powers constantly to evade authorities, thus giving him time to regain his composure. It remains to be seen his other intentions within the Foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I really don't know if calling an MTF squad for containment would really be necessary, considering that the level of threat was not fully known. Perhaps yes for he being a serial killer? Because he has already proven that he can do whatever goes on in his head without being stopped.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

