			<div class="content" id="post-content-4805376">
									

<p>Holy crap, I absolutely freakin' love this idea.</p>
<p>And now I must explain why I cannot grant you a Greenlight just yet.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Let&nbsp;us&nbsp;start&nbsp;the&nbsp;crit!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Let's&nbsp;do&nbsp;it!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Now, my thought process is very&#8230;how should I say it&#8230;fast and slow at the same time, so please forgive me if I ramble a bit.</p>
<p>Before we begin, I have to say this: the way you wrote this in your concept pitch was kinda awkward to pick through. You put part of the story with the <strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>, part of the story in the <strong>Central Narrative</strong>, and the rest in the <strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber</strong> and <strong>Additional Notes</strong>. But I won't bug you too much with that.</p>
<p>So first, let's start with the <strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>. I really dig it. It's an object that grants wish fulfilment-based superpowers. It's simple, but the possibilities are absolutely endless. You could write anything with this. Literally anything.</p>
<p>That said, the <strong>Central Narrative</strong>.</p>
<p>I really like it for the most part, but I spotted some weirdnesses (sorry, my vocabulary today is a little off) that I'd like to address.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The story is narrated by the author of the diary: a serial killer who spared the life of the overwhelmingly attractive man.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So&#8230;the serial killer was the author of the diary? As in he wrote it originally? And then the doctors had it for some reason and then the serial killer got it back?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The superpower had then passed on to the serial killer, even tho they had no blood connection.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, does he end up getting the diary back or no? Or is the superpower just passed to him next because he was the original owner?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The serial killer gained the ability to &quot;read&quot; a person's entire life by looking at their face, as well as being able to predict all outcomes of any interaction he exerts with them, which informs perfect place, time and method to kill them without a trace.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is the part that caught me. This is horrifying. Not to mention, instead of just having Evil Murder McBadPerson, you decided to make him have internal turmoil with his own humanity. That said, gonna have to figure how to make that bit work without having it feel forced.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He stopped the murders and dedicated the last days of life trying to seal his powers within the diary's last page by using his blood</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is this&#8230; actually how the thing works or is the serial killer just delusional?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>he believed in the existence of an afterlife in which he could continue to use these powers</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So he wants to keep killing in an afterlife where everyone's already dead? This bit's a headscratcher and a half&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He could escape the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Tbh considering he can just use his predictive outcome powers to get away with anything, he could just get away from the Foundation whenever he wished. Unless it was purely the moral problem that was eating away at him.</p>
<p>I do wanna know how he ended up gaining empathy after gaining these powers anyways.</p>
<p>Did he end up seeing that many people's lifetimes that he realized the magnitude of taking human life?</p>
<p>Feel free to PM me once you cleared up all of these.</p>
<p>I hope I helped and I bid you a lovely day, partner!</p>
<p>👍</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>EDIT:</strong></p>
<p>So, I was PMed with more information on this idea and I do still think it has a lot of promise, but after I read <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/riemann" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1787775); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1787775&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1603814304" alt="Riemann" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1787775)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/riemann" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1787775); return false;">Riemann</a></span>'s crit on this, I feel kinda silly not thinking of those issues earlier.</p>
<p>In terms of light status, it is not quite green, not yet. I'd say you're sitting at a steady yellow right now. My sides of the issue are fixed, I'd say. I just ask that you add everything I read in your PM into your concept post and make it neater to read, then follow up on Riemann 's crit.</p>
<p>I think I've done all I can now. Good luck with your idea, mate!</p>

							</div>

								
