			<div class="content" id="post-content-4805436">
									

<p>How does the Foundation fit into this story? What does this <em>look</em> like as an article?</p>
<p>Keep in mind that part of the challenge is figuring out how to present these stories. As it stands right now, you've got a couple distinct problems. How on earth does the serial killer find out about the rich family's ability? How does the Foundation know?</p>
<p>Same questions about how the Foundation knows about the serial killer or the diary - which feels like a rather convenient macguffin through which to tell the story.</p>
<p>Why would the Foundation care about a random dead corpse with a book full of crazy ranting?</p>
<p>You've got a lot of information that would be difficult to impossible for the Foundation to reasonably know, but you've not told us how any of this comes to be known or how it will be presented. I'm not even sure what the description of this would look like.</p>

							</div>

								
					
